[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4577990636","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119879#issuecomment-4577990636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119879","id":4577990636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEN6X7A","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T17:30:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T17:30:19Z","body":"Try doing an `await get_tree().physics_frame` just before freeing the object that causes the breakage, and running Physics Interpolation enabled, that may help.\n\nI've encountered this issue and these two things have helped me before I ditched TAA, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104622 also mentions this free problem but started focusing on the tickrate mismatch scenario as I was able to test that a lot better.\n\nFixing either issue will likely fix both, and this has been a problem since 4.4 and I believe possibly earlier as well.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4577990636/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4578527847","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119879#issuecomment-4578527847","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119879","id":4578527847,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEObKZw","user":{"login":"kubaofc123","id":17231482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjMxNDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17231482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123","html_url":"https://github.com/kubaofc123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kubaofc123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T18:23:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T18:23:39Z","body":"> Try doing an `await get_tree().physics_frame` just before freeing the object that causes the breakage, and running Physics Interpolation enabled, that may help.\n> \n> I've encountered this issue and these two things have helped me before I ditched TAA, [#104622](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104622) also mentions this free problem but started focusing on the tickrate mismatch scenario as I was able to test that a lot better.\n> \n> Fixing either issue will likely fix both, and this has been a problem since 4.4 and I believe possibly earlier as well.\n\n\nThat seems to work but only for simplest of scenes. As soon as there is more geometry, this method doesn't seem to do anything and bug persists. I think it would be best to find root cause in source code rather than try doing a workaround here","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4578527847/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4578782101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119879#issuecomment-4578782101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119879","id":4578782101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEOqrlQ","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T18:52:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T18:52:36Z","bod